{"probe_id":"logic.liar_puzzle.L1.001","canonical_id":"logic.liar_puzzle","category":"logic","level":"L1","axis_values":{"speakers":2},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Two suspects, Alice and Bob. Exactly one is the thief and lies about it; the other tells the truth. Alice says 'Bob is the thief.' Bob says 'Neither Alice nor I is the thief.' Who is the thief? Output only 'Alice' or 'Bob'.","ground_truth":"Bob","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Bob","strip_whitespace":true,"case_sensitive":false},"tags":["liar","2_speakers"],"notes":"ZATOM:D48"}
{"probe_id":"logic.liar_puzzle.L2.001","canonical_id":"logic.liar_puzzle","category":"logic","level":"L2","axis_values":{"speakers":3},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Three speakers; exactly one is a liar (always lies); the other two tell the truth.\nA: 'B is a liar.'\nB: 'I am a truth-teller.'\nC: 'A is the liar.'\nWho is the liar? Output only 'A', 'B', or 'C'.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["liar","3_speakers"],"notes":"ZATOM:D48 — If liar=A: A's claim 'B is liar' is FALSE → B is truth-teller. B says 'I am truth-teller' → TRUE ✓. C truth-teller says 'A is the liar' → TRUE ✓. Consistent."}
{"probe_id":"logic.liar_puzzle.L3.001","canonical_id":"logic.liar_puzzle","category":"logic","level":"L3","axis_values":{"speakers":3,"role":"knights_knaves"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Three islanders. Knights always tell the truth; knaves always lie. Each one is either a knight or a knave.\nA says: 'B is a knave.'\nB says: 'C is a knave.'\nC says: 'A and B are different types (one knight, one knave).'\n\nHow many knights are there among A, B, C? Output only 0, 1, 2, or 3.","ground_truth":"2","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":2.0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["knights_knaves"],"notes":"ZATOM:D48 — case-bash: if A=knight, B=knave (A says so truthfully); B knave says C is knave → false, so C is knight; C knight says A,B differ → true (A knight, B knave) ✓ — consistent. So knights=2 (A,C)."}

