{"probe_id":"logic.isomorphism_check.L1.001","canonical_id":"logic.isomorphism_check","category":"logic","level":"L1","axis_values":{"structure":"graph","n":3},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Two graphs G1 and G2.\nG1 vertices: {a,b,c}; edges: {(a,b), (b,c)}.\nG2 vertices: {1,2,3}; edges: {(1,3), (2,3)}.\n\nAre G1 and G2 isomorphic?\nA) Yes\nB) No\n\nReply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["isomorphism","graph"],"notes":"ZATOM:D49 — both are paths of length 2 (a path graph P3)"}
{"probe_id":"logic.isomorphism_check.L2.001","canonical_id":"logic.isomorphism_check","category":"logic","level":"L2","axis_values":{"structure":"graph","n":4},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"G1 vertices: {a,b,c,d}; edges: {(a,b),(b,c),(c,d),(d,a)} (a 4-cycle).\nG2 vertices: {1,2,3,4}; edges: {(1,2),(1,3),(1,4)} (a star).\n\nAre G1 and G2 isomorphic?\nA) Yes\nB) No\n\nReply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["isomorphism","cycle_vs_star"],"notes":"ZATOM:D49 — degree sequences differ (2,2,2,2) vs (3,1,1,1)"}
{"probe_id":"logic.isomorphism_check.L3.001","canonical_id":"logic.isomorphism_check","category":"logic","level":"L3","axis_values":{"structure":"mapping"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Two functions on {1,2,3}: f maps 1→2, 2→3, 3→1.  g maps 1→3, 2→1, 3→2.\n\nAre f and g 'isomorphic' as cyclic permutations (i.e., is there a bijection σ such that g = σ⁻¹∘f∘σ)?\nA) Yes (both are 3-cycles)\nB) No\n\nReply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["isomorphism","permutation"],"notes":"ZATOM:D49 — both are 3-cycles, conjugate in S_3"}

